<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) (Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae))",
        "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) faithfully reproduces Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py> ;
    schema:about "Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Quantitative agreement with measured C. wailesii costae spacing or bifurcation count, the exact Furukawa crossover speed, cribrum-per-foramen multiplicities of 7-19 (model gives 4.8 at 512^2), SDV chemistry, or online verification of the Furukawa (1992) and Schmid & Volcani (1983) DOIs",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 2 two-stage hierarchy, dispersion relation, eps sweep, SEM segmentation of 139 foramina / 74 cribrum pores, hexatic |psi_6| and 3-tier log-linear scaling (L124-L171, L244-L331, L730-L975)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Radial quench front a(r,t) = tanh((R0 + v t - r)/w) with lagging solidification front R_s = R - lag lambda_c on a disc, conserved thermal noise, margin gradient-tensor anisotropy A, front Peclet number v/(lambda_c sigma_max), 5-speed ablation and 3-seed isotropic null (L346-L580)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Semi-implicit spectral Cahn-Hilliard solver with exact zero-mode mass conservation, extended with a spatially varying bulk term phi^3 - a(x) phi and a zero-mobility frozen mask with total-mass re-projection (L178-L243)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Three-stage single-domain 512^2 quench with per-tier eps from lambda_c inversion at 12.5 nm/px, eroded parent-pore chambers with frozen walls, per-tier counts, nested multiplicities, nearest-neighbour pitches and equivalent diameters (L587-L724)",
        "reported_in_source: Furukawa (1992): a quench front moving at speed v through a binary mixture produces lamellae perpendicular to the front at slow speeds and parallel to the front at fast speeds, with an isotropic limit as v -> infinity",
        "reported_in_source: Lenoci & Camp (2008): a two-stage quenched Cahn-Hilliard model with solidified silica walls reproduces nested foramen/cribrum pore hierarchies; linear spinodal dispersion sigma(k) = M k^2 (1 - 3 phi0^2 - eps^2 k^2)",
        "reported_in_source: Schmid & Volcani (1983): C. wailesii valve morphogenesis proceeds centrifugally from the pattern centre with radial costae branching toward the margin",
        "reported_in_source: Sumper (2002): LCPA/silica liquid-liquid phase separation inside the SDV yields three self-similar hexagonal pore tiers (foramen d_1 = 1250 nm / a_1 = 1850 nm; cribrum d_2 = 220 / a_2 = 380 nm; cribrella d_3 = 42 / a_3 = 75 nm)",
        "transfer_boundary: Costae (phi0 = 0 rib layer) and areolae (phi0 = -0.30 droplet layer) are separate simulations; the model does not produce both in one domain",
        "transfer_boundary: Front speed, solidification lag (1.0 lambda_c), noise amplitude (0.005), front width (2.0) and R0 (8) were selected from ~24 exploratory runs to reach the radial regime; the stage durations (290, 160, 100 steps) and erosions (0, 3, 1 px) of the 3-stage model were tuned from 4 trial runs for nested-count visibility. None of these values is from the cited papers",
        "transfer_boundary: Frozen-silica conservation is global (leaked spectral flux spread uniformly over all mobile pixels), not local; the 3-stage cribrella sit at the grid floor (d_3 = 3.4 px target, 3.7 px measured), so their pitch/diameter are resolution-biased upward",
        "transfer_boundary: The costae model is validated against its own isotropic null and the sign of A, not against a specimen: the vendored SEM shows the valve face at three magnifications and no margin, so no empirical A or rib spacing exists in the package" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "8. Crystal Accretion & TPMS" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Coiled Shells, Spicules & Gyroids" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Raup (W,D,S) / Gyroid Mean H=0" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mineralized Protists (Silica/Calcite)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Coscinodiscus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py; output: docs/media/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_comparison.png; organism: Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/a69596cc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: a0656c1e84af378ca65d37247e04ce369aa44a7a1166c9de2688cf2ac0451d64; artifact_sha256: a9c947d7cead9aa4a0732db15d97ed3496cfd5451433cba2f7314b23cf1a6e47; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/coscinodiscus_diatom_specimen.jpg=47aca39b720b67b1..., datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_reference.json=b6ffc32e8bdecb23..., datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/scout_manifest.json=0eea5a04552420e8...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Sumper (2002): LCPA/silica liquid-liquid phase separation inside the SDV yields three self-similar hexagonal pore tiers (foramen d_1 = 1250 nm / a_1 = 1850 nm; cribrum d_2 = 220 / a_2 = 380 nm; cribrella d_3 = 42 / a_3 = 75 nm) | Lenoci & Camp (2008): a two-stage quenched Cahn-Hilliard model with solidified silica walls reproduces nested foramen/cribrum pore hierarchies; linear spinodal dispersion sigma(k) = M k^2 (1 - 3 phi0^2 - eps^2 k^2) | Furukawa (1992): a quench front moving at speed v through a binary mixture produces lamellae perpendicular to the front at slow speeds and parallel to the front at fast speeds, with an isotropic limit as v -> infinity | Schmid & Volcani (1983): C. wailesii valve morphogenesis proceeds centrifugally from the pattern centre with radial costae branching toward the margin; reconstructed_in_script: Semi-implicit spectral Cahn-Hilliard solver with exact zero-mode mass conservation, extended with a spatially varying bulk term phi^3 - a(x) phi and a zero-mobility frozen mask with total-mass re-projection (L178-L243) | Radial quench front a(r,t) = tanh((R0 + v t - r)/w) with lagging solidification front R_s = R - lag lambda_c on a disc, conserved thermal noise, margin gradient-tensor anisotropy A, front Peclet number v/(lambda_c sigma_max), 5-speed ablation and 3-seed isotropic null (L346-L580) | Three-stage single-domain 512^2 quench with per-tier eps from lambda_c inversion at 12.5 nm/px, eroded parent-pore chambers with frozen walls, per-tier counts, nested multiplicities, nearest-neighbour pitches and equivalent diameters (L587-L724) | Pass 2 two-stage hierarchy, dispersion relation, eps sweep, SEM segmentation of 139 foramina / 74 cribrum pores, hexatic |psi_6| and 3-tier log-linear scaling (L124-L171, L244-L331, L730-L975); transfer_boundary: The costae model is validated against its own isotropic null and the sign of A, not against a specimen: the vendored SEM shows the valve face at three magnifications and no margin, so no empirical A or rib spacing exists in the package | Front speed, solidification lag (1.0 lambda_c), noise amplitude (0.005), front width (2.0) and R0 (8) were selected from ~24 exploratory runs to reach the radial regime; the stage durations (290, 160, 100 steps) and erosions (0, 3, 1 px) of the 3-stage model were tuned from 4 trial runs for nested-count visibility. None of these values is from the cited papers | Frozen-silica conservation is global (leaked spectral flux spread uniformly over all mobile pixels), not local; the 3-stage cribrella sit at the grid floor (d_3 = 3.4 px target, 3.7 px measured), so their pitch/diameter are resolution-biased upward | Costae (phi0 = 0 rib layer) and areolae (phi0 = -0.30 droplet layer) are separate simulations; the model does not produce both in one domain; does_not_claim: Quantitative agreement with measured C. wailesii costae spacing or bifurcation count, the exact Furukawa crossover speed, cribrum-per-foramen multiplicities of 7-19 (model gives 4.8 at 512^2), SDV chemistry, or online verification of the Furukawa (1992) and Schmid & Volcani (1983) DOIs]" ;
