<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The header maps R1/R2 to the functions that implement them and to Furukawa (1992) and Schmid & Volcani (1983); `simulate_radial_quench_costae` and `simulate_three_stage_hierarchy` carry long docstrings that state the mechanism, the scale-invariance argument for the tier time steps, the neutral-wall decision and the off-critical result (concentric-only for phi0 = -0.30); the math-KG YAML registers equations 4-5 with single-range `code_locus` pins that match the current file, and the two new Lean theorems are named in the header (+1). Deductions: the docstrings state the mechanism but not that lag 1.0, noise 0.005, width 2.0, R0 8, v 0.10, steps (290, 160, 100) and erode (0, 3, 1) were hand-picked from exploratory runs — the handoff note says so, the code does not (-3); `pore_centroids` / `bond_orientation_coherence` outputs (`radial_frame_coherence_margin`, `lab_frame_coherence_margin`) are computed for the lamellar rib layer, where they are ~0 and meaningless, and used by no panel or measurement — dead output fields (-2); the `--self-test` help text still says '8-check' (-1). Net 91 -> 92." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L405–L440: simulate_radial_quench_costae signature and docstring: mechanism stated; tuned values lag=1.0, noise=0.005, width=2.0, R0=8 not flagged as hand-picked <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L405-L440>",
        "models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L534–L535: radial_frame_coherence_margin / lab_frame_coherence_margin returned but unused by any panel or measurement (dead for the lamellar rib layer) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L534-L535>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) — Model fidelity to source: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The fourth-order Cahn-Hilliard PDE with exact Fourier zero-mode conservation, the analytical spinodal dispersion and the Lenoci-Camp two-stage quench are unchanged from v2 and the `a_field=None, frozen_mask=None` path is bitwise identical (Check 7). Pass 3 adds a genuine new mechanism rather than a template: a spatially varying bulk term phi^3 - a(x) phi (stable single well ahead of the front, spinodal behind) with a lagging zero-mobility solidification front, and the radial/concentric/isotropic transition emerges from the front speed with no imposed stripe pattern (+2). The 3-stage model uses the CH scale invariance (x -> Lx, eps -> L eps, t -> L^2 t) to set per-tier eps from Sumper's pitches, and the frozen parent silica is a physically motivated confinement (+1). Deductions: the frozen-pixel solidification is a projection in a periodic spectral solver — leaked flux is re-distributed uniformly over all mobile pixels, so conservation is global, not local, and across all chambers in the 3-stage run (-2); the neutral wall value (phi_wall = tier phi0) was chosen because a -1 wetting wall produced surface-directed rings, a modelling decision not from the paper (-1); costae and areolae remain separate simulations (-1). Six Lean 4 theorems (2 new: stability ahead of the front; monotone irreversible solidification front) verify with 0 sorry." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` now returns 14 reference-anchored measurements (7 new) and the new metrics are well-defined: the gradient-tensor anisotropy A in the outer-40% annulus, the front Peclet number, exact mass drift over 6800 steps, per-tier counts/pitches/diameters converted to nm, and inter-tier pitch ratio a_2/a_3 = 5.108 vs Sumper 5.067 and d_3 = 46.5 vs 42 nm are genuine literature comparisons (+). Deductions, and the reason this dimension falls: three of the seven new measurements use model-internal references — the margin anisotropy uses the model's own 3-seed isotropic null, the radial-minus-concentric contrast uses the analytic null 0, and the SEM row-coherence C_6 uses the isotropic simulation as the reference for a specimen value (roles inverted) — none is an empirical literature value (-4); the Pass 2 method/note strings still hard-code '24.01 px, CV=0.133 ... 34.80 px ... n=139' and 'relative error=2.1%' instead of computing them, and the Pass 2 |psi_6| reference 0.75 has no literature provenance (-3); the two-stage 'nested cribrum sub-pores per foramen' = 2.04 vs ref 7.0 is a large miss that no note discusses (-2); the isotropic null is estimated from 3 seeds with a standard deviation (0.11) comparable to its mean and the self-test tolerance |A| < 0.35 is loose (-1). Net 88 -> 86." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L1321–L1339: Margin anisotropy and contrast measurements reference the model's own null (-0.110) and the analytic 0, not an empirical value <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L1321-L1339>",
        "models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L1394–L1412: Pass 2 d_1/a_1 method string hard-codes 24.01 px / 34.80 px / n=139 and 'relative error=2.1%' (L1397, L1401); |psi_6| reference 0.75 (L1409) has no literature provenance <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L1394-L1412>",
        "models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L1424–L1432: Two-stage nested cribrum per foramen = 2.04 vs reference 7.0; miss not discussed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L1424-L1432>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-3-stage-512x512-quench-simulated-inter-tier-pitch-ratio-a-2-a-3-cribrum-cribrella>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-3-stage-512x512-quench-simulated-tertiary-cribrella-pore-diameter-d-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-3-stage-512x512-single-domain-quench-tertiary-cribrella-pores-per-cribrum-pore>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-cahn-hilliard-conserved-mean-order-parameter-phi-drift>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-cahn-hilliard-interfacial-thickness-sweep-wavelength-correlation-r-lambda-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-centrifugal-front-quench-radial-minus-concentric-morphology-contrast-a-v-0-10-a-v-0-40>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-centrifugal-front-quench-total-order-parameter-conservation-with-frozen-silica-mass-re-projection>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-centrifugal-precipitation-front-quench-margin-radial-anisotropy-a-at-slow-front-speed-v-0-10-px-t>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-coscinodiscus-wailesii-sem-foramen-diameter-to-pitch-ratio-d-1-a-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-coscinodiscus-wailesii-sem-foramen-row-long-range-coherence-c-6-vs-isotropic-cahn-hilliard-stage-1-quench>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-coscinodiscus-wailesii-sem-primary-foramen-6-fold-hexatic-order-psi-6>,
