<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) — MorphoEval overall 89.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) remediated evaluation of `2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py` (rubric-weighted overall 89.0/100, v2 89.3; unweighted dimension mean 89.6). Both v2 remediation items are closed as honest reduced models: the Cahn-Hilliard solver is now coupled to a radially advancing quench + lagging silica precipitation front (`simulate_radial_quench_costae`, L405-L538) and the emergent slow-front regime (A = +0.647 at v = 0.10, Pe = 0.045) gives radial bifurcating lamellae while fast fronts (A = -0.942 at v = 0.40) give concentric ones, against a 3-seed isotropic null of -0.110 +/- 0.112 — the Furukawa (1992) directional-quench transition in polar geometry; and an explicit 3-stage 512^2 single-domain quench (`simulate_three_stage_hierarchy`, L600-L713) resolves 12 foramina -> 48 cribrum -> 225 cribrella with a_2/a_3 = 5.108 (ref 5.067) and d_3 = 46.5 nm (ref 42). The remediation exposed the next layer of defects: the costae model has no specimen margin view to compare against, three of the seven new measurements use model-internal references, the new JSON is documentation-only (not SHA-pinned, not loaded), the two new DOIs are unverified offline, and the Pass 2 hard-coded SEM statistics strings and the circular `segmented_reference_metrics` parity check remain. Self-test PASS (11 checks, 30 s); Lean 6 theorems, 0 sorry. Overall 89.0/100 (faithfulness 88.1, reproducibility 91.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a69596cc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py at a69596cc, image/png, 1162913 B, 2775×2070 px, artifact_sha256 a9c947d7cead9aa4a0732db15d97ed3496cfd5451433cba2f7314b23cf1a6e47 (sha256 a9c947d7cead9aa4a0732db15d97ed3496cfd5451433cba2f7314b23cf1a6e47), spec_fingerprint a0656c1e84af378ca65d37247e04ce369aa44a7a1166c9de2688cf2ac0451d64. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a0656c1e84af378ca65d37247e04ce369aa44a7a1166c9de2688cf2ac0451d64; artifact_sha256: a9c947d7cead9aa4a0732db15d97ed3496cfd5451433cba2f7314b23cf1a6e47; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/coscinodiscus_diatom_specimen.jpg=47aca39b720b67b1..., datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_reference.json=b6ffc32e8bdecb23..., datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/scout_manifest.json=0eea5a04552420e8...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Sumper (2002): LCPA/silica liquid-liquid phase separation inside the SDV yields three self-similar hexagonal pore tiers (foramen d_1 = 1250 nm / a_1 = 1850 nm; cribrum d_2 = 220 / a_2 = 380 nm; cribrella d_3 = 42 / a_3 = 75 nm) | Lenoci & Camp (2008): a two-stage quenched Cahn-Hilliard model with solidified silica walls reproduces nested foramen/cribrum pore hierarchies; linear spinodal dispersion sigma(k) = M k^2 (1 - 3 phi0^2 - eps^2 k^2) | Furukawa (1992): a quench front moving at speed v through a binary mixture produces lamellae perpendicular to the front at slow speeds and parallel to the front at fast speeds, with an isotropic limit as v -> infinity | Schmid & Volcani (1983): C. wailesii valve morphogenesis proceeds centrifugally from the pattern centre with radial costae branching toward the margin; reconstructed_in_script: Semi-implicit spectral Cahn-Hilliard solver with exact zero-mode mass conservation, extended with a spatially varying bulk term phi^3 - a(x) phi and a zero-mobility frozen mask with total-mass re-projection (L178-L243) | Radial quench front a(r,t) = tanh((R0 + v t - r)/w) with lagging solidification front R_s = R - lag lambda_c on a disc, conserved thermal noise, margin gradient-tensor anisotropy A, front Peclet number v/(lambda_c sigma_max), 5-speed ablation and 3-seed isotropic null (L346-L580) | Three-stage single-domain 512^2 quench with per-tier eps from lambda_c inversion at 12.5 nm/px, eroded parent-pore chambers with frozen walls, per-tier counts, nested multiplicities, nearest-neighbour pitches and equivalent diameters (L587-L724) | Pass 2 two-stage hierarchy, dispersion relation, eps sweep, SEM segmentation of 139 foramina / 74 cribrum pores, hexatic |psi_6| and 3-tier log-linear scaling (L124-L171, L244-L331, L730-L975); transfer_boundary: The costae model is validated against its own isotropic null and the sign of A, not against a specimen: the vendored SEM shows the valve face at three magnifications and no margin, so no empirical A or rib spacing exists in the package | Front speed, solidification lag (1.0 lambda_c), noise amplitude (0.005), front width (2.0) and R0 (8) were selected from ~24 exploratory runs to reach the radial regime; the stage durations (290, 160, 100 steps) and erosions (0, 3, 1 px) of the 3-stage model were tuned from 4 trial runs for nested-count visibility. None of these values is from the cited papers | Frozen-silica conservation is global (leaked spectral flux spread uniformly over all mobile pixels), not local; the 3-stage cribrella sit at the grid floor (d_3 = 3.4 px target, 3.7 px measured), so their pitch/diameter are resolution-biased upward | Costae (phi0 = 0 rib layer) and areolae (phi0 = -0.30 droplet layer) are separate simulations; the model does not produce both in one domain; does_not_claim: Quantitative agreement with measured C. wailesii costae spacing or bifurcation count, the exact Furukawa crossover speed, cribrum-per-foramen multiplicities of 7-19 (model gives 4.8 at 512^2), SDV chemistry, or online verification of the Furukawa (1992) and Schmid & Volcani (1983) DOIs." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py:1297-1318 and 540-566 — measure_morphoeval() ignores --N/--seed/ --v-front/--N3/--nm-per-px, the C4 sweep uses a fixed 5-speed list, and the isotropic null uses the median-speed step count with only 3 seeds (sd 0.11 ~ mean). Honour the CLI in the measurement block, use the slow-speed step count for the null, and raise the null to >= 8 seeds so the self-test tolerance |A| < 0.35 (L1536) can be tightened.",
        "remediation needed: 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py:1394-1412 and 1261 — the d_1/a_1 method string hard-codes '24.01 px, CV=0.133 ... 34.80 px, CV=0.075 ... n=139' and 'relative error=2.1%', the |psi_6| reference 0.75 (L1409) has no literature source, and the GIF title hard-codes '(139 foramina)'. Compute every number from `spec`, cite or remove the 0.75, and discuss the two-stage 2.04 vs 7.0 cribrum-per-foramen miss (L1424-L1432) in its note.",
        "remediation needed: 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py:19-24 and datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/paper_citations.bib:45-67 — the Furukawa (1992) and Schmid & Volcani (1983) DOIs were transcribed offline and not verified; verify them (and the 'Furukawa transition' regime assignment) when network access is available and clear the doi_verified_online flags.",
        "remediation needed: 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py:228-238 and 489-496 — frozen-silica conservation is a global re-projection of leaked spectral flux onto all mobile pixels (across all chambers in the 3-stage run). Replace with a conservative finite-volume variable-mobility update (M = 0 on frozen pixels) so conservation is local, and report per-chamber drift instead of the eroded-mask diagnostic.",
        "remediation needed: 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py:405-440 and 600-633 — the costae parameters (solidify_lag_lambda=1.0, noise_amp=0.005, front_width=2.0, R0=8, v_front=0.10) and the 3-stage stage durations (290, 160, 100 steps) and erosions (0, 3, 1 px) were hand-picked from exploratory runs to reach the radial regime / visible nesting; the docstrings state the mechanism but not the tuning. Flag each value as tuned in the docstring and the new JSON, and add a lag/noise sweep (or a 1D front-speed scan in v and lag) so the radial-concentric crossover is reported as a phase boundary rather than a single point.",
        "remediation needed: 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py:534-535 and 1571 — radial_frame_coherence_margin / lab_frame_coherence_margin are returned but unused (meaningless for the lamellar rib layer), and the --self-test help still says '8-check'. Remove or gate the dead fields behind a droplet-regime check and update the help text; also animate the 3-stage 512^2 run (the growth GIF still shows only the Pass 2 two-stage 128^2 run).",
        "remediation needed: 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py:600-713 — at 12.5 nm/px the cribrella are 3.4 px (grid floor; d_3 measured 3.7 px = 46.5 nm vs 42) and the domain holds only 12 foramina with 4.8 cribrum each (Sumper 7-19). Run a >= 1024^2 grid or <= 6 nm/px and a stage-2 duration/composition sweep, and add a resolution-convergence measurement for d_3 and a_3.",
        "remediation needed: 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py:86-117 and datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/centrifugal_front_three_stage_reference.json — the new reference table is neither in EXPECTED_SHA256 nor read by the script, so the Pass 3 parameters are traced only to source code. Pin it, load it in verify_and_load_reference(), and drive the costae/3-stage defaults and the self-test tolerances from it.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/coscinodiscus_diatom_specimen.jpg and 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py:1319-1339 — no vendored specimen shows the C. wailesii valve margin, so the costae anisotropy A and the radial-minus- concentric contrast are referenced to the model's own isotropic null and the analytic 0. Vendor a SHA-256-pinned margin/costae SEM (e.g. Schmid & Volcani 1983 plates), measure rib spacing vs radius and the bifurcation count, and replace the model-null references with the specimen values." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) — Parameter expressivity: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 adds a real control axis with a morphological transition: the 5-speed front ablation v in {0.05, 0.10, 0.20, 0.40, 0.80} px/t sweeps A from +0.65 (radial) through -0.94 (concentric) toward the isotropic null (panel C4), and `bulk_control=True` is a clean null (+2); the 3-stage model exposes grid size and physical scale (`--N3`, `--nm-per-px`) and `--v-front` drives panel C3 and the costae GIF (+1); the Pass 2 eps sweep, phi0 regimes and CLI flags remain. Deductions: `measure_morphoeval()` ignores every CLI parameter (fixed N = 128/160/512, seed 2002, v = 0.10/0.40) so the measurement block is not re-parameterisable from the command line (-2); the C4 sweep and the isotropic null use a fixed 5-speed list and the null's step count is the median-speed count, not the slow-speed count (-1); the costae parameters (lag 1.0, noise 0.005, width 2.0, R0 8) are exposed as function kwargs but not as CLI flags (-1). Net 86 -> 89." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L1297–L1318: measure_morphoeval() hard-codes N=128/160/512, seed 2002 and v=0.10/0.40; CLI parameters are not honoured by the measurement block <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L1297-L1318>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic RNG (seed 2002), 11-check `self_test()` (3 new: front-quench exact conservation, frozen subset of quenched, slow A > 0.15 / fast A < 0 / |null| < 0.35 at 96^2; 3-stage 256^2 strict nesting, decreasing pitches, pores within chambers, drift < 5e-3, eps-inversion parity; frozen-mask solver holds wall values bitwise) passes in 30 s; the `a_field=None` solver path is bitwise identical to Pass 2 so the Pass 2 determinism check still holds; the default render regenerates the 12-panel PNG, the two-stage GIF (byte-identical) and the new costae GIF in ~50 s; `three_stage_cached()` avoids recomputing the 512^2 run (+2). Deductions: `docs/media/*.png` is gitignored so the regenerated comparison PNG is not tracked (the measurements file records its SHA instead) (-1); the 3-stage 512^2 run has no animation — the growth GIF still animates only the Pass 2 128^2 two-stage run (-1); the self-test's single-realisation null tolerance |A| < 0.35 is loose relative to the 3-seed null spread. Net 90 -> 92." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-repro-package-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-repro-package-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) — Source and data traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Pass 2 package is intact: `verify_and_load_reference()` SHA-256-verifies the reference JSON, the SEM specimen and the scout manifest at every run, and the bib carries the four original DOIs. Pass 3 adds Furukawa (1992) and Schmid & Volcani (1983) to the header, the bib and the new JSON with a `doi_verified_online: false` flag and a provenance note that separates literature values from `model_prediction` rows (+ honest). Deductions, and the reason this dimension falls: the two new DOIs were transcribed from memory and could not be verified because network tools were disabled; the regime assignment 'Furukawa (1992) transition' is from memory and the crossover speed is a model prediction (-2); the new `centrifugal_front_three_stage_reference.json` is neither SHA-256-pinned in `EXPECTED_SHA256` nor read by the script — it is documentation-only, so the costae/3-stage parameters are traced to the script source, not to a verified dataset artifact (-2); the `segmented_reference_metrics` block of the Pass 2 JSON is the script's own Pass 2 output and the self-test asserts equality with it (circular, unchanged from v2) (-1); the Pass 2 `|psi_6|` reference 0.75 still has no cited source (already penalised above). Net 93 -> 90." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/centrifugal_front_three_stage_reference.json L1–L82: Pass 3 parameter/tier table with provenance_note and doi_verified_online: false; not SHA-pinned and not loaded by the script <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/centrifugal_front_three_stage_reference.json#L1-L82>",
        "models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L1506–L1512: Check 6 asserts parity with segmented_reference_metrics, which are the script's own Pass 2 outputs (circular) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L1506-L1512>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Pass 2 SEM segmentation of the SHA-256-locked C. wailesii valve (139 foramina, d_1/a_1 = 0.690 vs 0.6757, |psi_6| = 0.764; 74 cribrum sub-pores) is unchanged and the comparison figure now has 12 panels with the SEM panels B1/B2 beside the new 3-stage composite (C1) and a one-foramen zoom with a 200 nm scale bar (C2) that can be read against the SEM cribrum tier; the C3 disc visually resembles radial costae striation. Deductions, and the reason this dimension falls: the vendored specimen shows the valve face at three magnifications and NO valve margin, so the entire costae remediation (R1) has no specimen to match — its only reference is the model's own isotropic null (-5); the 3-stage model gives 4.8 cribrum per foramen versus Sumper's 7-19 and 5.0 cribrella per cribrum versus 7, and the Pass 2 two-stage run still gives 2.04 cribrum per foramen (-3); at 12.5 nm/px the tertiary pores are 3.4-3.7 px wide so panel C2's cribrella are at the grid floor (-2); the GIF right panel still hard-codes '(139 foramina)' as a title string rather than the segmented count (-1). Net 87 -> 85." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/centrifugal_front_three_stage_reference.json L1–L82: specimen gap recorded: no margin / costae view in the vendored SEM; the A reference is the model's isotropic null (model_prediction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/centrifugal_front_three_stage_reference.json#L1-L82>",
        "models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L1261–L1261: GIF right-panel title hard-codes '(139 foramina)' instead of the segmented count <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L1261-L1261>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

